<title>USA: Rubin bank plan constructive-House Banking's Leach.</title>
<headline>Rubin bank plan constructive-House Banking's Leach.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. House Banking Committee Chairman James Leach called a White House plan to modernize the nation's bank regulation laws &quot;very constructive,&quot; despite his differences over several key points.</p>
<p>&quot;While differences of judgment on several key legislative points remain, (Treasury) Secretary (Robert) Rubin's statement today is very constructive to the process,&quot; the Iowa Republican said.</p>
</text>
